Radio-frequency silicon-on-insulator (RF SOI) wafers are specialized semiconductor substrates used to manufacture radio-frequency components for wireless communication and connectivity systems. These engineered wafers help improve electrical isolation and reduce parasitic effects in devices such as RF switches and antenna tuners, supporting the performance requirements of modern mobile and connected technologies.

According to SemiconductorInsight, the global RF SOI Wafer Market was valued at USD 279.9 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 474.5 million by 2034, growing at a CAGR of 6.0% during 2026–2034. Asia Pacific is the largest regional market, supported by smartphone production, RF front-end manufacturing, specialty foundries and semiconductor-materials supply chains.

